counterfactuals.output:
An accordion door system comprising:

a plurality of elongated door panels arranged side-by-side and movable between an extended condition and a folded condition;

each of said panels including a longitudinal edge portion having a groove extending substantially along the length of the panel and an extension flange projecting from the edge portion;

a plurality of hinge members disposed between adjacent panels, each hinge member including interengaging hinge knuckles configured to permit pivotal movement of one panel relative to an adjacent panel;

wherein at least one of the hinge knuckles includes a tongue received within a corresponding longitudinal groove of a respective panel;

and wherein the tongue includes or cooperates with a flared wedge portion configured to engage the groove and/or the extension flange to retain the hinge member against withdrawal from the panel edge;

such that adjacent panels are hingedly connected by the engagement of the tongues and flared wedge portions with the grooves and extension flanges, thereby enabling controlled accordion-style folding and unfolding of the door system while maintaining alignment and retention of the hinge connection along the longitudinal edges of the panels.
